.Dd February 5, 2026
.Dt SH 1
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm sh
.Nd command interpreter (shell)
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl c Ar string
.Op Ar file
.Op Ar args ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility is a command interpreter that executes commands read from standard input or from a file.
.Pp
The shell implements a subset of the POSIX shell standard, including control structures, variable expansion, and input/output redirection.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl c Ar string
Read commands from the
.Ar string
operand instead of from the standard input.
.El
.Sh BUILTINS
The following built-in commands are supported:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Ic cd Op Ar directory
Change the working directory.
.It Ic exit Op Ar status
Exit the shell with the specified status.
.It Ic export Ar name Ns = Ns Ar value
Set an environment variable.
.It Ic read Op Fl r Ar var ...
Read a line from standard input.
.It Ic unset Ar name
Unset a variable/function.
.It Ic shift Op Ar n
Shift positional parameters.
.It Ic exec Op Ar command ...
Replace the shell with the specified command.
.It Ic . Ar file
Execute commands from a file in the current shell environment.
.El
.Sh PROMPT EXPANSION
If the
.Ev PS1
environment variable is set, it is expanded for the primary prompt.
Expansion occurs in the following order:
.Bl -enum
.It
Backslash escape sequences are replaced (POSIX mode).
.It
If Extended Mode is enabled, percent escape sequences are replaced.
.It
Parameter expansion, command substitution, and arithmetic expansion are performed.
.El
.Ss POSIX Mode (Default)
The following backslash escape sequences are supported:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Ic \e!
The current history command number.
.It Ic \e$
The character
.Ql #
if the effective UID is 0 (root), otherwise
.Ql $ .
.It Ic \e\e
A literal backslash.
.It Ic \eh
The hostname of the system (short form).
.It Ic \eu
The username of the current user.
.It Ic \ew
The current working directory, with
.Ev HOME
replaced by
.Ql ~ .
.El
.Ss Extended Mode
Extended Mode is enabled by setting:
.Dl set -o promptvars
.Pp
In Extended Mode, additional percent escape sequences are available.
.Pp
.Em Dynamic Elements:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Ic %n
The username of the current user.
.It Ic %m
The hostname (short form, up to first dot).
.It Ic %M
The full hostname.
.It Ic %~
The current working directory, with
.Ev HOME
replaced by
.Ql ~ .
.It Ic %#
The character
.Ql #
if the effective UID is 0 (root), otherwise
.Ql % .
.It Ic %?
The exit status of the last command.
.It Ic %L
The shell nesting level (from
.Ev SHLVL ) .
.It Ic %j
The number of background jobs.
.El
.Pp
.Em Styling & Attributes:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Ic %F{color}
Set foreground color. Supported colors: black, red, green, yellow, blue, magenta, cyan, white, default.
.It Ic %f
Reset foreground color to default.
.It Ic %K{color}
Set background color. Same colors as foreground.
.It Ic %k
Reset background color to default.
.It Ic %B
Enable bold text.
.It Ic %b
Disable bold text.
.It Ic %U
Enable underline.
.It Ic %u
Disable underline.
.El
.Pp
.Em Conditional Tokens:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Ic %(?<sep>true<sep>false)
Conditional based on exit status. If last command succeeded, expand to
.Ar true ,
otherwise
.Ar false .
The separator
.Ar <sep>
is any single character.
.It Ic %(#<sep>root<sep>user)
Conditional based on UID. If UID is 0, expand to
.Ar root ,
otherwise
.Ar user .
.El
.Pp
.Em Literal Percent:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Ic %%
A literal percent sign.
.El
.Ss SAFETY LIMITS
To prevent denial of service attacks and runaway expansion:
.Bl -bullet
.It
Maximum recursion depth: 10 levels.
.It
Maximum output size: 64KB.
.It
Signals (SIGINT, SIGTERM, SIGCHLD) are blocked during prompt expansion.
.El
Unknown escape sequences are printed literally.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The
.Nm
utility exits 0 on success, and >0 if an error occurs.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr udf 4
.Sh STANDARDS
The
.Nm
utility is designed to be compliant with the IEEE Std 1003.1-2008 ("POSIX.1") specification.
.Sh AUTHORS
The Substrate Project Developers.
